Cell["\<\
Three events, one per edge. They are distinct as events but isomorphic as \
hypergraphs, which CanonicalHypergraph makes plain:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6517453a-6fd3-7a43-8abb-b6e4011dfd73"],

Cell["\<\
Length @ DeleteDuplicates[CanonicalHypergraph[#[\"Hypergraph\"]] & /@ \
sub[star]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"02f8d5b7-db11-6f45-88cc-cffc2ab109b9"],

Cell[BoxData["1"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"f28df3f3-6363-764b-a9a9-63b520fc2669"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Distinct events with isomorphic results is the ordinary situation, not a \
special case, and it is why a multiway system has to decide whether its \
states are hypergraphs or isomorphism classes of them. The pieces for either \
reading are already here."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"64e69806-b1f0-9148-98c6-506454b58f01"],

Cell["An unordered rule", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5cdd2490-4463-2549-add2-787748c6ba18"],

Cell["\<\
Nothing about rewriting is particular to directed edges. Here an unordered \
pair becomes an unordered triple:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7067a735-5e37-6544-84e9-f3be9f881950"],

Cell["\<\
grow = HypergraphRule[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"]},
                      {Edge[{1, 2, 3}, \"Unordered\"]}];
Length @ grow[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"]}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6898bfe0-0106-a445-8e79-dcb2cd23c296"],

Cell[BoxData["2"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"acd2edcf-8a3f-c745-917e-6c9bc54727ec"],

Cell["\<\
Two events, from the two orderings the unordered pattern admits, and their \
results are the same hypergraph:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46b417bb-e4d3-3d41-88bb-61a6221ad703"],

Cell["\<\
DeleteDuplicates[#[\"Hypergraph\"] & /@ grow[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e8d1330d-b497-ed46-a74e-dfb831af6937"],

