  PlotRangePadding->Scaled[0.02]]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"13d4024e-4233-\
c946-9fab-6034a94d2d7a"],

Cell["8. Scope and limits", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5fb08f9f-713e-ff4d-916a-2bd6853478f9"],

Cell["\<\
What is here is the core: a rule, the matches of its input, and the events an \
application produces. Everything built on top of that \[LongDash] applying a \
rule over and over to collect the states it reaches, the graph of which event \
enabled which, and the conditions for two events to be independent \
\[LongDash] is in CausalityBasics.nb, and HypergraphRewritingSystem is where \
it starts.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a28cc56a-45e4-a94e-b1a5-7f117a3274f1"],

Cell["\<\
The matcher is a backtracking search over the edges of the input, and makes \
no attempt to be clever. Subhypergraph matching is hard in general, and the \
sizes this package is meant for are small; a rule with many edges against a \
large hypergraph will be slow, and that is the cost to watch.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"539aa8d0-b2c3-fa4e-9524-231ff973cd5f"],

Cell["\<\
The syntax follows the reference paclet: HypergraphRule[input, output], \
applied by rule[hg], giving associations keyed \"Hypergraph\", \
\"MatchVertices\", \"MatchEdges\" and the rest. Rules written for that paclet \
read the same here. The matcher underneath is this package's own, the \
reference's resting on a cloud resource function and on its own annotation \
system.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4521d582-eae4-6743-8c65-b85ede280ce7"],

Cell["\<\
The file tests/RewritingExamples.wls runs the examples in this notebook as \
assertions, plus invariants checked over three hundred events from rules \
built to match: that the binding really carries the input's edges onto the \
ones the match claims, that the edge counts add up, that nothing reported \
destroyed survives, and that the edges the rule did not touch are still there.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c4d2411a-e9df-a941-a660-ae303025cec1"],

Cell["\<\
Next: the plex diagrams that tie rewriting to hypermatrix algebra.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f307578-4335-5746-8908-c338bf4cb5da"]
},
